---
import LegalLayout from '../components/legal/LegalLayout.astro';
import LegalIdentity from '../components/legal/LegalIdentity.astro';
import { CUSTOM, FOUNDING_CLIENT, LICENCE_TERMS } from '../data/catalog';
import { SITE, businessName } from '../data/site';

const lastUpdated = new Date('2026-10-11');

const toc = [
  { id: 'who-we-are', label: '1. Who we are' },
  { id: 'these-terms', label: '2. These terms' },
  { id: 'website', label: '3. Using this website' },
  { id: 'quotes', label: '4. Quotes and orders' },
  { id: 'payment', label: '5. Prices and payment' },
  { id: 'scope', label: '6. Scope and changes' },
  { id: 'your-part', label: '7. Your part' },
  { id: 'acceptance', label: '8. Revisions and acceptance' },
  { id: 'ownership', label: '9. Who owns what' },
  { id: 'warranty', label: '10. Warranty' },
  { id: 'third-parties', label: '11. Hosting and third parties' },
  { id: 'ai', label: '12. AI features' },
  { id: 'hardware', label: '13. Hardware' },
  { id: 'data', label: '14. Personal data' },
  { id: 'liability', label: '15. Limits of liability' },
  { id: 'confidentiality', label: '16. Confidentiality' },
  { id: 'ending', label: '17. Cancelling and ending' },
  { id: 'founding-clients', label: '18. Founding Client Programme' },
  { id: 'complaints', label: '19. Complaints and disputes' },
  { id: 'changes', label: '20. Changes to these terms' }
];
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Terms"
  description="The terms for using the WSS DevLabs website and for our websites, systems, custom builds and Care Plans: payment, scope, ownership, warranty, liability and disputes."
  path="/terms/"
  lastUpdated={lastUpdated}
  intro="Plain-language terms for using this website and for working with us. Your quotation or Statement of Work sets out the specific scope, price and timeline for your project."
  toc={toc}
>
  <h2 id="who-we-are">1. Who we are</h2>
  <p>These terms are between you and {businessName} ("we", "us").</p>
  <LegalIdentity />

  <h2 id="these-terms">2. These terms</h2>
  <p>
    These terms apply to everything we sell: websites, ready-made systems, custom builds, add-ons and Care Plans. Ready-made systems
    are also covered by our <a href="/licence/">Licence Agreement</a>, and Care Plans by the <a href="/care-plan-terms/">Care Plan
    terms</a>. Larger projects may also have a Master Services Agreement and schedules such as a Data Processing Agreement.
  </p>
  <p>
    If documents conflict, this order applies: your quotation or Statement of Work, then any schedules, then a Master Services
    Agreement, then these terms. Nothing in these terms takes away rights you have by law, for example as a consumer under the
    Consumer Protection Act 1999.
  </p>

  <h2 id="website">3. Using this website</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Articles and guides on this site are general information, not professional advice for your situation.</li>
    <li>Prices on this site are current prices. The price that binds us is the one in your quotation or order confirmation.</li>
    <li>The text, design and code of this website belong to us. Please don't copy them without permission.</li>
    <li>Links to other websites are for convenience. We're not responsible for their content.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="quotes">4. Quotes and orders</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Quotations are valid for 30 days.</li>
    <li>
      A project starts when you accept the quotation in writing (a signature, an e-signature, or a clear written "accepted",
      including on WhatsApp) and pay the first payment.
    </li>
    <li>
      Ready-made systems are ordered through an order request on this site. We email an invoice; once payment clears, we send the
      download link, licence and install guide.
    </li>
    <li>Your quotation lists everything included. Anything not listed is not included.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="payment">5. Prices and payment</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Prices are in Ringgit Malaysia and are final. No SST is added.</li>
    <li>
      Payment schedules: One-Page and Business websites 50% to start and 50% before going live; Store websites 40% / 30% / 30%;
      custom builds 30% to start, 40% at the staging demo and 30% at handover; ready-made systems in full before download; Care Plans
      monthly or yearly in advance.
    </li>
    <li>Invoices are due within 7 days. Late payment interest may apply at the rate stated in your quotation.</li>
    <li>If a payment is more than 14 days late, we may pause work and support after giving you written notice.</li>
    <li>We hand over source code, credentials and ownership once everything due has been paid.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="scope">6. Scope and changes</h2>
  <p>
    We deliver the items listed in your quotation or Statement of Work. Anything else is a change. Changes get a written change
    request with a fixed price and the effect on the timeline, and work only starts once you approve it. We never bill for changes
    after the fact.
  </p>

  <h2 id="your-part">7. Your part</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Provide the content, information and access listed in your quotation within the agreed time. Delays on your side move the timeline.</li>
    <li>If we don't receive what we need for 30 days, we may pause the project, invoice the work completed, and reschedule when you're ready.</li>
    <li>Name one person who can make decisions and reply within 2 working days.</li>
    <li>Make sure you have the rights to the content you give us (text, photos, logos) and the consents needed for any personal data you collect.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    You agree to cover us for claims caused by content or data you provide, or by using what we deliver in breach of the law.
  </p>

  <h2 id="acceptance">8. Revisions and acceptance</h2>
  <p>
    Each package lists its revision rounds. When we deliver a draft, staging site or milestone, please test it and either approve
    it or list the specific problems within 5 working days. If we hear nothing in that time, or you start using it live, it counts
    as accepted. We fix listed problems that fall within the agreed scope.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ownership">9. Who owns what</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Websites and custom builds:</strong> once you've paid in full, you own the design, code and content we created
      specifically for you.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Our building blocks:</strong> we keep our own templates, components, code libraries and know-how that existed before
      your project or were made independently of it. You get a permanent, royalty-free licence to use them as part of what we
      delivered to you.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Ready-made systems:</strong> you get a perpetual licence with the full source code, not ownership of the product. See
      the <a href="/licence/">Licence Agreement</a>.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Third-party and open-source parts</strong> stay under their own licences, which we list in a notice file at handover.</li>
    <li><strong>Your domain</strong> is registered in your name, and we hand over every login when the project ends.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="warranty">10. Warranty</h2>
  <p>
    After acceptance we fix, free of charge, anything we built that doesn't work as described in your quotation: One-Page websites
    for 14 days, Business and Store websites for 30 days, ready-made systems for {LICENCE_TERMS.supportDays} days and custom builds
    for {CUSTOM.build.warrantyDays} days.
  </p>
  <p>
    The warranty doesn't cover changes made by others, third-party services, hosting you manage, hardware, or misuse. Software is
    never completely free of errors, and we don't promise it will be. We target a 90+ mobile Lighthouse score at handover on the
    agreed content, and fix it free if we miss. We never guarantee search rankings, because Google decides them.
  </p>

  <h2 id="third-parties">11. Hosting and third parties</h2>
  <p>
    Some features rely on third-party services such as hosting, domain registries, payment gateways, WhatsApp and AI providers. Their
    availability, prices and terms are outside our control. Their usage fees are paid by you, at cost, unless your quotation says
    otherwise.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">12. AI features</h2>
  <p>
    AI-generated answers can be wrong. You approve the knowledge base an AI assistant uses. Users are always told they're talking to
    an automated assistant and can reach a person. AI assistants must not be used to give medical, legal or financial advice.
  </p>

  <h2 id="hardware">13. Hardware</h2>
  <p>
    Hardware we supply comes with the manufacturer's warranty only. We're not responsible for losses caused by device failure, power
    or network outages, or alerts that aren't acted on. You remain responsible for insuring your premises, stock and equipment.
    Electrical and cabling work is carried out by licensed contractors.
  </p>

  <h2 id="data">14. Personal data</h2>
  <p>
    Our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Notice</a> explains how we handle personal data. Where we process personal data on your behalf,
    you are the data controller and we are the data processor, acting only on your instructions under a Data Processing Agreement.
  </p>

  <h2 id="liability">15. Limits of liability</h2>
  <p>
    Our total liability for each project is limited to the fees you paid for that project. For Care Plans, it is limited to the fees
    paid in the previous 12 months. For ready-made systems, it is limited to the licence fee you paid.
  </p>
  <p>
    Neither of us is liable for indirect or consequential losses, such as lost profits, revenue, goodwill, or data beyond what can be
    restored from our latest backup. Nothing in these terms limits liability for fraud, or anything else that cannot be limited by
    law.
  </p>

  <h2 id="confidentiality">16. Confidentiality and staff</h2>
  <p>
    We each keep the other's confidential information private, and use it only for the project, during the project and for 3 years
    afterwards. We're happy to sign a mutual NDA before you share anything sensitive. During a project and for 12 months afterwards,
    neither of us will directly hire the other's staff or contractors who worked on it without consent.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ending">17. Cancelling and ending</h2>
  <p>
    Refunds and cancellations follow our <a href="/refunds/">Refund Policy</a>. Either of us may end an agreement if the other
    seriously breaches it and doesn't fix the breach within 14 days of written notice. You pay for work done up to that point, and we
    hand over the completed work you've paid for. Neither of us is liable for delays caused by events beyond reasonable control, such
    as natural disasters, major provider outages or government action, as long as we tell each other promptly.
  </p>

  <h2 id="founding-clients">18. Founding Client Programme</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Our first {FOUNDING_CLIENT.totalSlots} clients after our relaunch get {FOUNDING_CLIENT.discountPercent}% off{' '}
      {FOUNDING_CLIENT.appliesTo}. It doesn't apply to {FOUNDING_CLIENT.excludes}.
    </li>
    <li>
      In return, within 30 days of launch, you agree to give us: a case study interview with real results, permission to publish
      your business name, logo and approved screenshots, an honest public review, and a 15-minute feedback call.
    </li>
    <li>You approve the case study text before we publish it. Screenshots use sample data or are blurred where needed.</li>
    <li>
      We ask for an honest review. The discount never depends on the review being positive.
    </li>
    <li>If the case study, permission and review aren't provided, the discount amount becomes payable.</li>
    <li>The programme ends when all {FOUNDING_CLIENT.totalSlots} places are taken.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="complaints">19. Complaints and disputes</h2>
  <p>
    If something isn't right, tell us at <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. We acknowledge complaints within 2
    working days and give a full response within 10 working days.
  </p>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of Malaysia. If a dispute can't be settled by talking, we will try mediation, for example
    through the Asian International Arbitration Centre, before going to the courts of Kuala Lumpur. Consumers may also bring
    claims to the Tribunal for Consumer Claims Malaysia.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">20. Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms. The version that applies to your project is the one in force when you accepted your quotation. The
    date at the top shows the latest version.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
